contentText:
Caleb Flynn , the former American Idol contestant accused of fatally shooting his wife, has been found guilty of murder.

An Ohio jury reached the verdict Tuesday (Sept. 29) after about 2.5 hours of deliberation, determining that the 40-year-old musical pastor is guilty on all charges, which span aggravated murder and multiple counts of murder, felonious assault and tampering with evidence in connection with the death of his wife, Ashley Flynn. Going into the trial, Caleb had pleaded not guilty.

