Following the court&#8217;s decision, defense attorney Patrick Mulligan told reporters , &#8220;While we respect the system, certainly we&#8217;re disappointed &#8230; there&#8217;s a lack of evidence on prior calculation and design.&#8221;

Caleb was charged in February with murdering Ashley &#8212; with whom he shares two daughters &#8212; after she died via gunshot in their Tipp County home earlier that month. After the shooting, he&#8217;d called 911 and told the dispatcher that a burglary had taken place and that the intruder had been the person who killed his wife.

Text messages read in court, however, showed that Caleb had been having a 1.5-year affair with now-24-year-old Alleigha Botner, who worked at his church as an intern and gave hours of testimony during the trial. “If I could literally kill her and not go to hell, I would do it in a heartbeat,” Caleb texted Botner in May 2025, according to CNN . &#8220;That’s how dark and hateful I feel.&#8221;

The exchanges also showed Botner asking Caleb to get a divorce from Ashley so that they could be together instead. On Feb. 15, the day before the shooting, Caleb &#8212; having told Botner that he was planning to tell Ashley he was leaving her the following day &#8212; sent in a message: “It’s kind of crazy. I’m not scared tomorrow. I mean, I’m not looking forward to it, and it’s about to be a crap-fest here moving forward, but I’m not scared of it.&#8221;

Caleb made it as far as the televised judges&#8217; auditions on the 12th season of American Idol in 2013, but did not advance to the main competition. In his &#8220;Road to Hollywood&#8221; interview for the TV show, he repeatedly mentioned his love for Ashley, his marriage to whom lasted about 16 years before her murder.

&#8220;I love to sing, so that&#8217;s why I auditioned &#8212; and my wife kind of nudged me a little bit too,&#8221; he said in the clip. &#8220;I love my wife more than anything. She is very, very pretty.&#8221;

